            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>[Column A] To the Perpetual Augustan Health, and the Public Liberty of the Roman People.
                   [Column B] To the Genius of the municipium in the 704th year after the founding of Interamna, when Gnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus [and] [[[Camillus Arruntius Scribonianus]]] were consuls.
                   [Footer] For the Providence of Tiberius Caesar Augustus, born for the eternity of the Roman name, after the most pernicious enemy of the Roman people have been removed, Faustus Titius Liberalis, sexvir Augustalis again, took care to have this erected at his own expense.
                </p>
